and Events On-Campus Recruiting Post an Employment Opportunity Sponsorships FAQ: Hiring International Students Workforce Training Alumni Information Family Information Faculty and Staff Information Life Design Partner Hall of Fame Award Personnel Request More Info Apply to IUP Welcome to the Career and Professional Development Center! We look forward to connecting with you and are committed to providing quality services and developmental opportunities that support the educational objectives of IUP. Our goal is to teach students, by providing career consultation and support, how to become active participants in their own continuing career development. Information for Students Find information on the services we offer. Information for Employers Find information on our events and how to connect with our students. Schedule an Appointment Schedule an appointment with a member of the CPDC team. Events Attend our upcoming events. Internships and Jobs Explore internship and job opportunities. Professional Resources Check out these helpful resources. Stay up to date with programming and services, receive valuable career information and tips, and ask career-related questions by following our social media accounts! Twitter: @IUPCPDC Instagram: @IUPCPDC TikTok: @IUPCPDC Facebook: @IUPCPDC LinkedIn Groups: IUP Career Development and Networking + IUP Alumni YouTube: IUP Career and Professional Development Center News IUP to Host Internship Summit for Local Employers The Career and Professional Development Center at IUP invites employers from Armstrong, Butler, and Indiana counties to join us for an Internship Summit on Tuesday, October 20, 2026. 31 August 2026 IUP Students Complete Career and Leadership Skills Academy at S&T Bank Five students at Indiana University of Pennsylvania were selected for the 2026 Career and Leadership Skills Academy, a strategic collaboration between the PA Bankers Association, IUP, Shippensburg University, Commonwealth University, and Kutztown University. 26 August 2026 New Workplace Essentials Certificate Program Helps Professionals Build In-Demand Career Skills Professionals looking to strengthen their workplace effectiveness and advance their careers have a new opportunity to develop the skills employers value most. The Workplace Essentials Certificate program, a new noncredit training initiative, launched its first cohort in May 2026. 07 July 2026 A Strong Spring Semester Starts with the CPDC The IUP CPDC supports students at every stage of their career journey, from exploring majors and career paths to applying for internships, jobs, and graduate programs. 14 January 2026 IUP Career and Professional Development Center Recognizes Outstanding Faculty and Organizational Partners With Hall of Fame Awards Indiana University of Pennsylvaniaâs Career and Professional Development Center has announced its fall 2025 Outstanding Organizational Partners, who join the CPDCâs Partner Hall of Fame. 19 November 2025 Career and Professional Development Center B20 Stabley Library 429 South Eleventh Street Indiana, PA 15705 Phone: 724-357-2235 career-development@iup.edu Fall and Spring Office Hours Monday, Thursday, Friday 8:00 a.m.–4:30 p.m. Tuesday and Wednesday 8:00 a.m.–7:00 p.m. Fall and Spring Drop-In Express Hours Monday 10:30 a.m.–12:30 p.m. Tuesday and Wednesday 4:00–7:00 p.m. Exceptions to Normal Hours Wednesday, April 29: Closed at 4:30 p.m. https://iup.studentadvisor.ai/virtualadvisor Resources for Prospective Students Current Students Faculty and Staff Alumni and Friends Parents News and Media Quick Links Apply Now Campus Tours Athletics Libraries Colleges and Departments Find People Support & Safety Academic Support Health and Well-Being IT Support Emergency Information Report an Incident of Concern Accessibility Questions Connect MyIUP Email D2L 1011 South Drive Indiana, PA 15705 Phone: 724-357-2100 Contact Us Maps & Directions Fraud, Waste, and Abuse Hotline Student Complaints Net Price Calculator Right to Know Â© 2007-2026 Indiana University of Pennsylvania"
